    "title": "Memorial storms back late to take down Castle - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Ayden Crowley ,\n1 hours ago NEWBURGH, Ind. (WEHT) — The Memorial Tigers remain unbeaten in the SIAC after a 3-1 victory over the Castle Knights. The Tigers trailed 1-0 at the half but 3 second half goals helped lift them over the Knights.\nMemorial looks to continue its winning ways on Sept. 19 against St. Xavier (Louisville). Meanwhile, Castle looks to bounce back on Sept. 20 against Floyd Central.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to Eyewitness News (WEHT/WTVW).",
